WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.418
Host: Explain why a single tongue map cannot
replace a modality-specific answer.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:14.647
Guide: General sensation, taste and movement
use different pathways. Most anterior general
sensation uses V3,

3
00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:20.530
Guide: anterior taste uses VII, posterior
sensation and taste use IX,

4
00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:28.658
Guide: and most motor supply uses XII.
Circumvallate papillae and palatoglossus are
important exceptions.

5
00:00:28.658 --> 00:00:34.262
Host: Which exception should accompany an
anterior-versus-posterior tongue taste map?

6
00:00:34.262 --> 00:00:38.601
Guide: Circumvallate papillae receive taste
fibres from IX.

7
00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:45.254
Guide: Circumvallate papillae lie just
anterior to the terminal sulcus but have IX
taste innervation.
